"""
A release's changelog as structured data.

This is the contract between a non-deterministic producer — a person or a
language model reading commits, pull requests and diffs — and the
deterministic consumers that render it. Authoring may vary between runs;
rendering may not. Every published artifact (a `CHANGELOG.md` section, a
forge release body) is rendered from one instance of this type, so no two
artifacts describing the same release can disagree.

`proposedBump` carries the author's conclusion about release impact. It is
a proposal, never an authority: the release tooling computes the bump
independently from commit metadata and halts when the two disagree.
"""
struct Changelog {
    """
    Version of this schema that the instance conforms to.

    Consumers reject an instance declaring a schema version they do not
    implement rather than rendering it partially.
    """
    schemaVersion: String

    """
    The release impact the author concluded from the content.

    Compared against the bump the tooling computes from commit metadata.
    A disagreement halts the release for human confirmation; it is never
    resolved by preferring one side.
    """
    proposedBump: Bump

    """
    The resolved version this changelog describes, without a tag prefix —
    for example `1.4.0`.

    Left unset while a changelog is being authored, and filled in once the
    version is resolved. Renderers require it, because a rendered section
    is headed by the version it describes.
    """
    version: String?

    """
    A short headline for the release, at most one sentence.

    Rendered above the entries where a target supports it. Omitted for
    releases that carry no theme worth naming — most patch releases.
    """
    title: String?

    """
    One or two paragraphs introducing the release in prose.

    This is where a release earns readable notes: what changed in aggregate,
    who should care, and what to do about it. Entries carry the itemized
    record; this carries the narrative.
    """
    summary: String?

    """
    The itemized record of what changed, in the order it should be rendered.

    Renderers group entries by `kind` and preserve this order within each
    group, so authoring order is presentation order.
    """
    entries: [ChangelogEntry]

    """
    Release-level breaking changes and the migrations they require.

    Declared here, rather than only on the entries that cause them, so that
    a migration spanning several changes can be described once. An entry may
    still set its own `breaking` flag and carry a narrower migration note.
    """
    breakingChanges: [BreakingChange]

    """
    Which inputs this changelog was authored from.

    Recorded so a reader can tell whether the notes were written from commit
    subjects alone or from pull-request descriptions and diffs, and so a
    regeneration can reproduce the same inputs.
    """
    sources: [ChangelogSource]
}

"""
A single itemized change.
"""
struct ChangelogEntry {
    """
    What kind of change this is. Determines which section renders it.
    """
    kind: ChangeKind

    """
    One line stating the change from the reader's point of view.

    Written as an outcome a consumer can recognize, not as the work that
    produced it: "closed decoders reject undeclared keys", not "refactored
    the decoder".
    """
    summary: String

    """
    The part of the product this change affects, in the project's own
    vocabulary — for example `transpilers/go` or `cli`.

    Rendered as a prefix where a target supports it. Unset where a change is
    not scoped to one area.
    """
    scope: String?

    """
    Additional prose for a change that cannot be understood from its
    summary alone.

    Rendered beneath the summary. Most entries need none.
    """
    detail: String?

    """
    Whether this change alone breaks a consumer that upgrades.

    An entry may be breaking without a corresponding `BreakingChange` on the
    release, in which case `migration` carries the whole of the guidance.
    """
    breaking: Bool

    """
    Pull request numbers this change arrived through.

    Rendered as links where the target supports it.
    """
    pullRequests: [Int]

    """
    Commit identifiers this change arrived through.

    Full hashes; renderers abbreviate. Carried for entries that reached the
    release outside a pull request.
    """
    commits: [String]

    """
    Issue or work-item identifiers this change resolves, in the tracker's own
    form — for example `strata-8da` or `#412`.
    """
    issues: [String]

    """
    What a consumer must do to adopt this change, where anything is required.

    Set only where `breaking` is true, or where adoption is optional but
    non-obvious.
    """
    migration: String?
}

"""
A breaking change described at release level, spanning one or more entries.
"""
struct BreakingChange {
    """
    One line stating what no longer works the way it did.
    """
    summary: String

    """
    What a consumer must do to upgrade.

    Required: a breaking change without migration guidance is an incident
    report, not a release note.
    """
    migration: String

    """
    Pull request numbers that together constitute this breaking change.
    """
    pullRequests: [Int]
}

"""
An input a changelog was authored from.
"""
struct ChangelogSource {
    """
    Which adapter produced the input — for example `git-commits`,
    `forge-pull-requests` or `diff`.
    """
    adapter: String

    """
    The range or locator the adapter read, in the adapter's own form — for
    example `v1.3.0..HEAD`.
    """
    reference: String

    """
    How many records the adapter contributed.

    Lets a reader tell an empty source from an absent one.
    """
    recordCount: Int
}

"""
The release impact of a change or of a release as a whole.
"""
enum Bump {
    """
    Breaks a consumer that upgrades without changes.
    """
    MAJOR

    """
    Adds capability while remaining compatible.
    """
    MINOR

    """
    Corrects behaviour without adding capability.
    """
    PATCH

    """
    Nothing a consumer of the published artifacts would observe.
    """
    NONE
}

"""
The category of an itemized change, which decides the section it renders in.
"""
enum ChangeKind {
    """
    New capability a consumer can use.
    """
    FEATURE

    """
    A correction to behaviour that was wrong.
    """
    FIX

    """
    A change whose observable effect is speed or resource use.
    """
    PERFORMANCE

    """
    A capability that has been withdrawn.
    """
    REMOVAL

    """
    A documentation change a consumer would look for in release notes.
    """
    DOCUMENTATION

    """
    A dependency version change a consumer may need to know about.
    """
    DEPENDENCY

    """
    A change with no consumer-visible effect, recorded for completeness.
    """
    INTERNAL
}
